{"title":"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e138091c36351769959c8ab6e5bbb46705bf8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^a+2^b=3^c+3^d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />, the number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> which can possibly be negative, is, at most:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2def83c19f81784fe22a9a1ddd9e5a7d4a58eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a23bd1f771175c201ac14f56c6cfe0b3dab0fd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,d \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8362e1f78725beb1de44c30360f0a10d0d3c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e1900f9ae83cebcbb5735f6c7bd6b6c505ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />.  This also takes into account when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is negative.  That means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4dee8a5ec7b9cf786358b16d3491def9d98cee3b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2^{-a}} + 2^b = 3^c + 3^d\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" />\nMultiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e51d5da8ef10d21d9ff8681e432473b8362658a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-a}$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f15d341dfc75029f83cae9e17949c13e5c274790.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 2^{-a+b} = 2^{-a} (3^c + 3^d)\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\nNote that both sides are integers.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3c11a9c0b3b892676261e6c765abdd58cc2b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ne b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, then the right side is even while the left side is odd, so equality can not happen.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/657f0df041b95da1a42a90a66afe7678b50b1944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-a} (3^c + 3^d) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />, and since  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef8362e1f78725beb1de44c30360f0a10d0d3c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/35496101e151991fc3213a7472ade63fd75bdf8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0f154fee9f3975e2758b8a1b16f68c92811f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^c + 3^d = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />.  No nonnegative value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> works, so equality can not happen.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> can not be negative when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a23bd1f771175c201ac14f56c6cfe0b3dab0fd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,d \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a4544432ca43ada42d0ef4cbaa7ba968f40fd43d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, and WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3dd417591a694e2339db5d9c3666343ee396e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da395499c40b6f23ec1473c6296931a8d49abd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\le d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />.  This also takes into account when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is negative.  That means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/9339bb1852b25882cdeea245c14c0a7b43b29f84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^a + 2^b = \\frac{1}{3^{-c}} + 3^d\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"37\" />\nMultiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f636774bd9673c65805e6c1511b315ecf6deb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{-c}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/47665ffba27649bbeda956197d048d1accedd3ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^{-c} (2^a + 2^b) = 1 + 3^{d-c}\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />\nThat makes both sides integers.  The left side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the right side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so equality can not happen.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can not be negative when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a4544432ca43ada42d0ef4cbaa7ba968f40fd43d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28a0a8ab2b9b8a80fc9d2a716ecef8a037905672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,c &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, and WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e1900f9ae83cebcbb5735f6c7bd6b6c505ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da395499c40b6f23ec1473c6296931a8d49abd1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\le d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />.  This also takes into account when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is negative.  That means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d578af58164cb3d4fc6a903e2c36541b038076b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2^{-a}} + 2^b = \\frac{1}{3^{-c}} + 3^d\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />\nMultiply both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b70f6c114537590dd48546ba951f24f3d3445f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-a} \\cdot 3^{-c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5b3d70ca12e9107d40897d68c1b1abe70b30f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3^{-c} (1 + 2^{b-a}) = 2^{-a} (1 + 3^{d-c})\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"20\" />\nThat makes both sides integers.  The left side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the right side is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so equality can not happen.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> can not be negative.\n</p><p>Putting all the information together, none of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> can be negative, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME\" title=\"1963 AHSME\">1963 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1963 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1963\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">26</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">27</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">28</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">29</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 30\">30</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">31</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">32</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">33</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 34\">34</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_35\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 35\">35</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 36\">36</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 37\">37</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 38\">38</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_39\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 39\">39</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_40\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 40\">40</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AHSME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AHSME Problems and Solutions\"> All AHSME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017012433\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.184 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 390/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2984/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 196/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9391/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   30.259      1 -total\n 82.55%   24.980      1 Template:AHSME_40p_box\n 16.69%    5.049      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser